; MAC-HYG-11: a template's free identifier naming a function its
; module keeps private is refused AT THE INVOCATION, with AX3023,
; not at the definition. `helper` resolves where `once` is defined
; (same module, MAC-HYG-6/7), and the expansion carries it here,
; where it does not exist. The mirror - a private *macro* - is
; refused at the definition site instead (MAC-LANG-10).
(import PrivMac)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (once 21))
